# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal notes -- this repo is public
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTES.md holds the operational history that does not belong in a world-readable
# repo: GPU allocations on the shared box, incident forensics, and the older
# private tree this one was split out of. The physics rationale and every measured
# number live in MANIFEST.md instead -- none of that was removed.
NOTES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model run outputs (this project)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A single 90-day run writes ~5 GB of .npz per checkpoint cycle; the tree this
# repo replaced accumulated 30 GB of them and became unusable. The patterns are
# broad ON PURPOSE -- outputs land in whatever directory you launch from, under
# names keyed by OUT_TAG, so a prefix-only rule (coupled_*) misses them.
*.npz
*.png
*.gif
*.pid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# runs/ and outputs/ -- the two directories that exist to hold things git must
# never see
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# runs/<TAG>/ is raw model output (~5 GB per checkpoint cycle on a 90-day run);
# outputs/ is what plotting and analysis derive from it. Both are reproducible
# from the model plus a tag, so neither belongs in history.
#
# The pattern is `runs/*`, NOT `runs/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so the trailing-slash form would make the `!` exception below
# unreachable and the READMEs -- which are the only record of what each
# directory is for -- would vanish from a fresh clone.
runs/*
!runs/README.md
outputs/*
!outputs/README.md
